---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '../layouts/main.astro';
import { ContactForm } from '../components/ContactForm';
---

<Layout
  title="Contact"
  description="Contact Freddie Philpot about cybersecurity work experience, projects or technology opportunities."
>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <h1>Contact</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="contact-grid">
      <div>
        <a class="contact-email" href="mailto:contact@freddiephilpot.dev">
          contact@freddiephilpot.dev
        </a>
        <p>
          I’m looking for cybersecurity work experience alongside my A-levels.
          If you have an opportunity, a question about a project, or something
          useful to share, I’d like to hear from you.
        </p>
        <div class="social-links">
          <a
            class="text-link"
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/freddiephilpot/"
          >
            LinkedIn ↗
          </a>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/pphilfre">
            GitHub / pphilfre ↗
          </a>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/philfreddie">
            Lab write-ups / philfreddie ↗
          </a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/cv.pdf">
            Download CV (PDF) ↗
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ContactForm client:visible />
    </div>
    <section class="case-section">
      <h2>Before getting in touch</h2>
      <div class="skill-rows">
        <div>
          <h3>What experience am I looking for?</h3>
          <p>
            I’m interested in opportunities involving cybersecurity, software
            development or IT infrastructure alongside my A-levels. My previous
            placements included observing code reviews and security monitoring;
            I’d like to build on that exposure and understand how teams work in
            practice. My <a href="/certifications">experience page</a> explains
            what I did and which courses I’ve completed.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>What should a message include?</h3>
          <p>
            For a placement, include the team, location, proposed dates and time
            commitment, plus the kind of work I would observe or help with. For
            a project question, name the project and describe the behaviour
            you’re asking about. An example or a link to the relevant page helps
            make the question specific.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Where can I see evidence of the work?</h3>
          <p>
            The <a href="/projects">case studies</a> link to source code and
            explain implementation choices, tests and known limits. For example,
            Dispatch covers sync retries, Glyph covers ownership checks, and my
            home-lab notes describe DNS troubleshooting. Screenshots are
            labelled where they use sample or illustrative data.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>What if the form does not work?</h3>
          <p>
            The form needs JavaScript and a verification check. If verification
            cannot load or sending fails, email
            <a href="mailto:contact@freddiephilpot.dev">
              contact@freddiephilpot.dev
            </a>
            directly. A success message appears only after the server accepts
            the submission; entering text alone does not send it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
